  "body": "## Summary\n\n* **Goal:** Add StarDict `.syn` synonym-file support to the reader's dictionary lookup — the follow-up explicitly listed as \"deliberately cut\" in the Slim Dictionary PR (#2583).\n* **Changes:** Resolve alternate spellings and irregular forms (e.g. `theatre`→`theater`, `oxen`→`ox`) via a dictionary's optional `.syn` file, slotting in between the direct index match and the English stemmer in `Dictionary::lookup()`.\n\n**How it works.** A `.syn` entry carries an *ordinal* (the N-th `.idx` entry), not a byte offset. The existing `.qidx` sidecar already samples byte offsets at fixed entry-count boundaries, so it doubles as an ordinal→offset map: `locateByOrdinal()` reads sample `N / SAMPLE_INTERVAL` then scans the remainder. A parallel `.sidx` sidecar makes the `.syn` itself binary-searchable, mirroring `.qidx` over `.idx`. The sidecar header is generalized (`QidxHeader`→`SidecarHeader`) and gains an `entryCount` field to bounds-check ordinals; version bumped 1→2 so stale `.qidx` files auto-rebuild. **Zero new persistent RAM** — everything streams from SD reusing the existing scan buffer. All BE32 reads go through the existing byte-assembly helper (RISC-V alignment-safe).\n\n**Composing with #2733.** Rebased onto current `develop`, so this now builds on the `LookupSession` from *\"perf: open dictionary index files once per lookup\"* rather than reopening files per probe. All four search entry points (`locate`, `locateByOrdinal`, `locateSynonym`) take the session, so a synonym lookup adds **no** SD opens or `std::string` path temporaries to the hot path:\n\n* `.syn` / `.sidx` are opened **lazily**, by `openSynonyms()` on first use. Only an exact-match miss consults them, so a direct hit never pays for the two extra opens.\n* `buildSidecar()` propagates #2706's `IndexResult`, so an OOM during indexing still reports \"Not enough memory\" rather than a generic failure. The `.syn` pass is best-effort and passes `nullptr` — a failed synonym index disables synonyms for the session but cannot downgrade the build result or break the dictionary.\n* `sidecarIsStale()` checks each sidecar independently, so editing a `.syn` doesn't force a needless rescan of the (much larger) `.idx`, and vice versa.\n* `locateSynonym()` / `locateByOrdinal()` set `readError` on seek failure, preserving #2706's \"a search that never reached a verdict is not a miss\" contract.\n\n## Scope Check\n\nCrossPoint is intentionally narrow. See [SCOPE.md](../blob/develop/SCOPE.md) and [ROADMAP.md](../blob/develop/ROADMAP.md).\n\n- [x] I have read SCOPE.md and ROADMAP.md.\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new built-in theme.\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new external network connector.\n- [x] This PR is **not** an interactive app, writing tool, RSS/news/browser, media playback, or PDF feature.\n- [x] The stock firmware does not already handle this — it improves an already-in-scope feature (dictionary lookup, #917) by raising hit-rate on inflected/variant forms at ~zero RAM cost.\n- [x] Does **not** touch `freeink-sdk/`, `lib/hal/`, the bootloader, OTA, or recovery code — only `src/util/Dictionary.*`, a docs update, and a test fixture. No maintainer coordination required on that basis (happy to coordinate with the dictionary-area maintainers regardless — see below).\n\nThis is the `.syn` follow-up seam from #2583. Not currently on a ROADMAP milestone or the #1599 to-do list, so flagging for a maintainer nod. Rebased onto `develop` — #2733, #2706 and #2877 have landed since this was opened and are all preserved (see \"Composing with #2733\" above). Still aware of dictionary rework in flight (#2663, #2690, mcrosson's orchestration branch) — glad to rebase/coordinate again.\n\n## Additional Context\n\n* **Memory/flash impact:** No new persistent RAM. The per-lookup `LookupSession` is a stack local and grows by two `HalFile` handles plus three `uint32_t` — `HalFile` is pimpl with a defaulted constructor, so that is 16 bytes of stack and **zero heap** unless a miss actually opens the synonym files. Two additional small SD sidecars (`.sidx`, and the existing `.qidx` gains one `uint32`). Streaming-only; reuses the 256-byte scan buffer.\n* **Cache format:** `.qidx` version 1→2, so existing dictionaries re-index once on first open (existing \"Indexing dictionary…\" flow). Sidecars are safe to delete; they rebuild.\n* Docs updated in `docs/dictionary.md` (`.syn` moved from \"Not supported\" to supported, lookup order and per-sidecar rebuild documented).\n\n### Testing\n\nTested on device (X3). Using the **GNU Collaborative International Dictionary of English (GCIDE)** StarDict build — which ships an 11,466-entry `.syn` — from:\nhttps://tuxor1337.frama.io/firedict/dictionaries.html\n\nA test EPUB is included at `test/epubs/test_dictionary_synonyms.epub` (generator: `scripts/generate_dictionary_synonyms_test_epub.py`). Every word in it is a direct-index **miss** resolvable only through `.syn`, and also unreachable by the stemmer, so a hit exercises the synonym path specifically:\n\n| Look up | Resolves to |\n|---|---|\n| theatre | theater |\n| sceptre | scepter |\n| absinthe | absinth |\n| accoutre | accouter |\n| accurst | accursed |\n| abettor | abetter |\n| aardwolf | aard-wolf |\n\nControl words (`dog`, `cat`) are direct hits, confirming the reader isn't just failing everything. Verified each test word resolves to its headword on device; control words behave as before.\n\n**Post-rebase status:** builds clean (`pio run -e default`, 0 warnings) and clang-format clean. The on-device pass above was run before the rebase onto #2733's session refactor; re-verifying the synonym path and the one-time `.qidx` v1→v2 rebuild on hardware before merge.\n\n---\n\n### AI Usage\n\nDid you use AI tools to help write this code? _**YES**_ — implemented with AI assistance (design, code, and this test fixture); reviewed and tested on hardware by me.\n",
